            <div xml:id="d451">

                <pb facs="0376" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859B.01/190: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Godthaab</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Penfield</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-29T19:00:00-04:00">May 29, 1940—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Your 17, May 27, 11 p.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d451-f1"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Transaction concluded today and <hi rendition="#italic">Campbell</hi>
                        expected to sail tonight or tomorrow with arms mentioned in our 8, May 26, 3
                        p.m. on board. No publicity is being given here.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>We propose to have the <hi rendition="#italic">Campbell</hi> proceed
                        directly to Godthaab, there embarking Governor Svane and proceeding to
                        Ivigtut where Governor Svane would be in a position to determine the
                        distribution of the arms to reliable individuals. Please telegraph Governor
                        Svane’s opinion of this proposal which has the approval of the Danish
                        Minister.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
